VeridianOS: Predicate::toString(): no stray quote after a string list

Real bug (prepared for upstream, invent.kde.org/frameworks/solid):
a string-list value was written as "{'a', 'b'}'": the closing literal had
one quote too many, so toString() of such a predicate could not be parsed
back into the same predicate.

--- a/src/solid/devices/frontend/predicate.cpp
+++ b/src/solid/devices/frontend/predicate.cpp
@@ -294,7 +294,7 @@
             if (list.isEmpty()) {
                 value = QStringLiteral("{}");
             } else {
-                value = QStringLiteral("{'") + list.join(QStringLiteral("', '")) + QStringLiteral("'}'");
+                value = QStringLiteral("{'") + list.join(QStringLiteral("', '")) + QStringLiteral("'}");
             }
             break;
         }
